= Solution
{parent=2}

If $K=\{\lambda_0\}$, the <projection-valued measure> satisfies $P(\{\lambda_0\})=P(K)=I$. Its integral representation therefore reduces to
$$
\boxed{T=\int_Kz\,dP(z)=\lambda_0P(K)=\lambda_0I.}
$$
Thus a <normal operator> with a singleton spectrum is a scalar multiple of the <identity operator>. Normality is essential: a nonzero nilpotent matrix has spectrum $\{0\}$ but need not be zero.

